From bfe82d1aaf4ac042cc1f12aedd092fdbb14f47de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jodydadescott <jody@thescottsweb.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:22:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Images: stop pushing the deprecated tacplus image from this
 line (#932)

docs/VERSIONING.md on main says ghcr.io/tacplus-dev/tacplus/tacplus is
deprecated, its tags stay as they are and it is never pushed again (#193),
yet every patch on this line still built and pushed it (tacplus:2.3.24 on
2026-11-15), as root, in no security report and pinned by no fleet.

- images.yml: the tacplus and tacplus-manifest jobs are gone. A release
  still tags the build image it was produced with (X.Y.Z, X.Y, X by
  scripts/images-tags.sh), now in a build-tags job of its own; the dispatch
  input loses its tacplus choice.
- images/tacplus.Dockerfile and the dead root Dockerfile (#580) are gone;
  `just images` builds base and build only.
- Docs (VERSIONING, the README, the site's install page) say the image is
  deprecated and that tacplus:2.3 stays at 2.3.24: a consumer installs the
  release binary and keeps it current with `tacplus upgrade`.
- scripts/images_no_tacplus_test.go: images.yml builds, pushes and tags no
  tacplus image, its Dockerfiles are gone, and a release still tags its
  build image.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
